{number: 60}
{title: Break Thou the Bread of Life}
{key: Eb}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Eb] Break thou the bread of life, [Ab] dear Lord, to [Eb] me,
As thou didst [Cm] break the [Ab] loaves be-[Eb] side the [Bb7] sea;
[Eb] Beyond the sacred page I [Ab] seek thee, [Eb] Lord,
My spirit [Cm] pants for [Ab] thee, O [Eb] living [Bb7] [Eb] Word.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[Eb] Bless thou the truth, dear Lord, to [Ab] me, to [Eb] me,
As thou didst [Cm] bless the [Ab] bread by [Eb] Gali-[Bb7] lee;
[Eb] Then shall all bondage cease, all [Ab] fetters [Eb] fall;
And I shall [Cm] find my [Ab] peace, my [Eb] All in [Bb7] [Eb] all.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[Eb] Thou art the Bread of Life, O [Ab] Lord, to [Eb] me,
Thy holy [Cm] Word the [Ab] truth that [Eb] saveth [Bb7] me;
[Eb] Give me to eat and live with [Ab] thee a-[Eb] bove;
Teach me to [Cm] love thy [Ab] truth, for [Eb] thou art [Bb7] [Eb] love.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
O [Eb] send thy Spirit, Lord, now [Ab] unto [Eb] me,
That he may [Cm] touch mine [Ab] eyes, and [Eb] make me [Bb7] see:
[Eb] Show me the truth concealed with-[Ab] in thy [Eb] Word,
And in thy [Cm] Book re-[Ab] vealed I [Eb] see the [Bb7] [Eb] Lord.
{end_of_verse}
